n6w|n|The oval or roundish body laid by domestic poultry and other birds, tortoises, etc. It consists of a yolk, usually surrounded by the "white" or albumen, and inclosed in a shell or strong membrane. ; A simple cell, from the development of which the young of animals are formed; ovum; germ cell. ; Anything resembling an egg in form.	a:1cb7,140,2~1cb7,140,2	n:mu0,135,2~mu0,135,2	N:1lpj,47,3~1lpj,47,3
